    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d519">

                <pb facs="0525" n="516" xml:id="pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2231/232: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-14T14:00:00-04:00">May 14, 1938—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Your telegram no. 47, May 12, noon. The reasons set forth in instruction no.
                    301, April 15 why this Government could not accept in the proposed trade
                    agreement or in an exchange of notes the trade balance proviso suggested by
                    Ecuador, would obtain equally in respect of a unilateral declaration.
                    Accordingly you may inform the appropriate authorities that while the Department
                    is still prepared to agree to a 6 months cancellation clause which could be
                    invoked by Ecuador for any reason sufficient to itself, this Government cannot
                    consent to be placed on notice on signing the agreement that should the trade
                    balance between the two countries become “unfavorable” to Ecuador for reasons
                    beyond our control, Ecuador proposes to terminate the trade agreement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
